window.SEARCH_INDEX = [{"t":"Strata Mundi Wiki","u":"index.html","s":"Welcome Welcome to the Strata Mundi wiki, \"the layers of the world\"! It's a block-based building and exploration game: an endless world, calculated from a seed, for you to roam, dig and reshape as you please. For now (v0.1), you play in creative mode : every block is within reach, you can fly, and you build without limits. The world [LORE TO WRITE] Finding your way around the wiki Blocks : one page per block, with its infobox (identifier, category, properties), where to find it and how to use it. Biomes : the world's landscapes, their ground and their vegetation. Commands : everything the cons"},{"t":"What's new","u":"news.html","s":"Version 0.2.1 (2026-11-13) Lantern — Can also hang under a block, and drops if that block is broken. Torch — Can also be placed against a wall, and drops if that wall is broken. Liquids — Water heads for the nearest hole (4 blocks at most) instead of spreading everywhere; it reaches 7 blocks. Sounds — Every sound is ready from loading; lava can be heard, the wind is softer; Ambiences slider. World generation — Biomes two to three times larger; a hot and dry biome no longer touches a snowy one; rare, narrow ravines with bare rock walls. Changelog"},{"t":"Changelog","u":"changelog.html","s":"Version 0.2.1 (2026-11-13) Lantern — Can also hang under a block, and drops if that block is broken. Torch — Can also be placed against a wall, and drops if that wall is broken. Liquids — Water heads for the nearest hole (4 blocks at most) instead of spreading everywhere; it reaches 7 blocks. Sounds — Every sound is ready from loading; lava can be heard, the wind is softer; Ambiences slider. World generation — Biomes two to three times larger; a hot and dry biome no longer touches a snowy one; rare, narrow ravines with bare rock walls. Version 0.2.0 (2026-11-11) Badlands — Added Beach — Added "},{"t":"Acacia Leaves","u":"blocks/strata/acacia_leaves.html","s":"Description Olive green foliage, full of little holes the sky shines through. Obtaining In creative: the Natural tab of the inventory, or /give acacia_leaves . In the world, they form the crown of acacia trees in savannas . Usage Hedges, green roofs, gardens and tree houses in acacia colours. Behaviour A solid but see-through block. For now, leaves do not fall when you cut the trunk. Tips Their shade stands out from afar: handy to spot these trees from a hilltop. Discovery in game Aim at a tree crown to read its name, or search for \"leaves\" in the creative inventory. Generation In the vegetati"},{"t":"Acacia Log","u":"blocks/strata/acacia_log.html","s":"Description A acacia trunk with smooth grey bark, with bright orange rings at each end. Obtaining In creative: the Natural tab of the inventory, or /give acacia_log . In the world, it forms the trunks of acacia trees in savannas : a tree with a trunk that leans to one side before holding up a flat, wide crown like a parasol. Usage Beams, pillars, timber frames and cabins, with a colour of its own to vary your builds. Behaviour A full, opaque block. Like every log, it is oriented : placed on the top or bottom of a block, it stands upright; placed against the side of a block, it lies down along "},{"t":"Acacia Planks","u":"blocks/strata/acacia_planks.html","s":"Description Neatly lined-up acacia planks of bright orange wood. Obtaining In creative: the Building tab of the inventory, or /give acacia_planks . They are not found in the world: this is a building block. Usage Floors, walls, decks and timber frames; their colour sets them apart from oak and fir planks. Behaviour A full, opaque block. Tips A floor alternating two woods instantly makes a room look tidy. Discovery in game Search for \"planks\" in the creative inventory. History 0.2.0 Added"},{"t":"Bedrock","u":"blocks/strata/bedrock.html","s":"Description Bedrock is the floor of the world. A rough, dark, stubborn layer laid at the very bottom so that nothing slips out underneath. Obtaining In creative: the Natural tab of the inventory, or /give bedrock . In the world, it lines the bottom of every column: one continuous row at the very bottom, topped with a few scattered blocks that make its surface bumpy. Caves never carve into it. Usage In creative, it's a decorative block with plenty of character. In survival, it will be a hard limit: whatever lies beneath stays out of reach. Behaviour A full, opaque, motionless block. It is unbre"},{"t":"Birch Leaves","u":"blocks/strata/birch_leaves.html","s":"Description Soft green foliage, full of little holes the sky shines through. Obtaining In creative: the Natural tab of the inventory, or /give birch_leaves . In the world, they form the crown of birch trees in forests , among the oaks (and soon in birch forests). Usage Hedges, green roofs, gardens and tree houses in birch colours. Behaviour A solid but see-through block. For now, leaves do not fall when you cut the trunk. Tips Their shade stands out from afar: handy to spot these trees from a hilltop. Discovery in game Aim at a tree crown to read its name, or search for \"leaves\" in the creativ"},{"t":"Birch Log","u":"blocks/strata/birch_log.html","s":"Description A birch trunk with white bark streaked with black, with pale, almost creamy rings at each end. Obtaining In creative: the Natural tab of the inventory, or /give birch_log . In the world, it forms the trunks of birch trees in forests , among the oaks (and soon in birch forests): a tree tall and slender, with a narrow round crown. Usage Beams, pillars, timber frames and cabins, with a colour of its own to vary your builds. Behaviour A full, opaque block. Like every log, it is oriented : placed on the top or bottom of a block, it stands upright; placed against the side of a block, it "},{"t":"Birch Planks","u":"blocks/strata/birch_planks.html","s":"Description Neatly lined-up birch planks of pale, almost creamy wood. Obtaining In creative: the Building tab of the inventory, or /give birch_planks . They are not found in the world: this is a building block. Usage Floors, walls, decks and timber frames; their colour sets them apart from oak and fir planks. Behaviour A full, opaque block. Tips A floor alternating two woods instantly makes a room look tidy. Discovery in game Search for \"planks\" in the creative inventory. History 0.2.0 Added"},{"t":"Bookshelf","u":"blocks/strata/bookshelf.html","s":"Description Oak planks lined with colourful books. Stacked, bookshelves connect : the borders disappear and they make one big piece of furniture. How to get it In the creative inventory, Building tab. Behaviour A full block with planks on top and bottom. Its sides change with the bookshelves above and below (connected texture). It is flammable : fire catches it quickly. Tips The \"Texture variants\" graphics setting turns the connection off if you prefer separate blocks. Discovering it in game Stack three bookshelves: the furniture is drawn in one piece. History 0.2.0 Added"},{"t":"Brown Mushroom","u":"blocks/strata/brown_mushroom.html","s":"Description A small brown mushroom with a flat cap, discreet and a little shy, growing at the foot of trees. Obtaining In creative: the Plants tab of the inventory, or /give brown_mushroom . In the world, it is found in small groups in forests (more common than the red mushroom). Usage Decorating gardens, meadows and path edges; a touch of life around your builds. Behaviour A crossed plant: two crossing planes, visible from every side. It has no collision (you walk through it) and hides no neighbouring block. You can aim at it and break it in one hit; it does not grow or spread after the world"},{"t":"Brown Mushroom Block","u":"blocks/strata/brown_mushroom_block.html","s":"Description A piece of a giant brown mushroom cap, wide and flat like a table. Obtaining In creative: the Natural tab of the inventory, or /give brown_mushroom_block . In the world, it forms the flat cap of giant brown mushrooms, in the giant mushroom lands. Usage Platforms, flat roofs, giant picnic tables. Behaviour A full, opaque, soft block: it breaks quickly. Tips The top of a brown mushroom is a great lookout over the surroundings. Discovery in game Aim at a giant mushroom cap to read its name at the top of the screen. Generation In the vegetation: Mushroom Fields History 0.2.0 Added"},{"t":"Bush","u":"blocks/strata/bush.html","s":"Description A round, leafy bush, as tall as a sitting cat. Perfect for hiding, provided you are a cat. Obtaining In creative: the Plants tab of the inventory, or /give bush . In the world, it is found alone or in pairs in plains and forests , on grass. Usage Decorating gardens, meadows and path edges; a touch of life around your builds. Behaviour A crossed plant: two crossing planes, visible from every side. It has no collision (you walk through it) and hides no neighbouring block. You can aim at it and break it in one hit; it does not grow or spread after the world is generated. Tips Since it"},{"t":"Cactus","u":"blocks/strata/cactus.html","s":"Description The cactus, prickly king of the desert. Green, ribbed, bristling with spines, it grows bolt upright and never asks to be watered. The ideal housemate. Obtaining In creative: the Natural tab of the inventory, or /give cactus . In the world, it only grows in the desert, on sand , as small columns a few blocks tall, scattered among the dunes. Usage Desert decoration, dry gardens, very dissuasive fences (in looks, at least). Behaviour A solid, motionless block. For now, it doesn't prick : damage arrives with survival. It doesn't grow after the world is generated either, and in creative"},{"t":"Coal Ore","u":"blocks/strata/coal_ore.html","s":"Description Grey stone speckled with matte black spots: coal. It's the most common ore in the world, the one you bump into around every cave corner. Obtaining In creative: the Natural tab of the inventory, or /give coal_ore . In the world, it forms small veins in stone, over a very wide range of heights: from the depths right up into the mountainsides, where it sometimes shows in the open air. In deep stone, it takes the form of deep coal ore. Usage For now, it's a decorative block that looks nice in a stone wall. Ores can't be harvested yet : breaking one in creative simply makes it vanish. I"},{"t":"Copper Ore","u":"blocks/strata/copper_ore.html","s":"Description Stone dotted with small coppery orange flecks that catch the torchlight. Copper is iron's warm cousin: showier, and almost as common. Obtaining In creative: the Natural tab of the inventory, or /give copper_ore . In the world, it forms small veins in stone, halfway down under plains and hills. It also comes in bulk in the giant deposits of verdigris rock. In deep stone, it becomes deep copper ore. Usage A decorative block for now: ores can't be harvested yet , and breaking one in creative simply makes it vanish. Behaviour A full, opaque, motionless block, from the same family as st"},{"t":"Cornflower","u":"blocks/strata/cornflower.html","s":"Description A cornflower with star-shaped petals, of a bold blue found almost nowhere else. Obtaining In creative: the Plants tab of the inventory, or /give cornflower . In the world, it is found in the flower patches of the plains . Usage Decorating gardens, meadows and path edges; a touch of life around your builds. Behaviour A crossed plant: two crossing planes, visible from every side. It has no collision (you walk through it) and hides no neighbouring block. You can aim at it and break it in one hit; it does not grow or spread after the world is generated. Tips Since it blocks nothing, yo"},{"t":"Daisy","u":"blocks/strata/daisy.html","s":"Description A simple daisy, white petals and a yellow heart. It grows wherever the grass is soft. Obtaining In creative: the Plants tab of the inventory, or /give daisy . In the world, it is found in the flower patches of the plains . Usage Decorating gardens, meadows and path edges; a touch of life around your builds. Behaviour A crossed plant: two crossing planes, visible from every side. It has no collision (you walk through it) and hides no neighbouring block. You can aim at it and break it in one hit; it does not grow or spread after the world is generated. Tips Since it blocks nothing, y"},{"t":"Dandelion","u":"blocks/strata/dandelion.html","s":"Description A sunny yellow dandelion, the most common flower of the meadows. It seems to be smiling. Obtaining In creative: the Plants tab of the inventory, or /give dandelion . In the world, it is found in the flower patches of the plains (the most common one, with the poppy). Usage Decorating gardens, meadows and path edges; a touch of life around your builds. Behaviour A crossed plant: two crossing planes, visible from every side. It has no collision (you walk through it) and hides no neighbouring block. You can aim at it and break it in one hit; it does not grow or spread after the world i"},{"t":"Dead Bush","u":"blocks/strata/dead_bush.html","s":"Description A small dry bush with twisted branches, which gave up on leaves long ago. It still keeps its spirits up among the dunes. Obtaining In creative: the Plants tab of the inventory, or /give dead_bush . In the world, it is found here and there in the desert , on sand. Usage Decorating gardens, meadows and path edges; a touch of life around your builds. Behaviour A crossed plant: two crossing planes, visible from every side. It has no collision (you walk through it) and hides no neighbouring block. You can aim at it and break it in one hit; it does not grow or spread after the world is g"},{"t":"Deep Coal Ore","u":"blocks/strata/deep_coal_ore.html","s":"Description The deep version of coal ore: black spots set into deep stone, dark on dark. You need a sharp eye to spot it, but it's definitely there. Obtaining In creative: the Natural tab of the inventory, or /give deep_coal_ore . In the world, it appears instead of coal ore wherever a vein runs through deep stone, so in the depths of every biome. Usage A decorative block for now. Like every ore, it can't be harvested yet : in creative, breaking it makes it vanish without leaving anything behind. Behaviour A full, opaque, motionless block, from the same family as deep stone, and harder than it"},{"t":"Deep Copper Ore","u":"blocks/strata/deep_copper_ore.html","s":"Description Deep stone, dark and dense, with the same coppery flecks as copper ore. The contrast makes them even easier to spot. Obtaining In creative: the Natural tab of the inventory, or /give deep_copper_ore . In the world, it is copper ore wherever stone gives way to deep stone, in small veins as well as at the bottom of giant deposits. Usage A decorative block for now: ores can't be harvested yet . Behaviour A full, opaque, motionless block, harder than ordinary copper ore. Tips Giant deposits that dive below the deep stone line change colour on the way: follow the vein. Discovery in game"},{"t":"Deep Diamond Ore","u":"blocks/strata/deep_diamond_ore.html","s":"Description Sky-blue crystals set into deep stone, shining like stars in an ink-black sky. This is the form in which diamond truly shows itself in the world. Obtaining In creative: the Natural tab of the inventory, or /give deep_diamond_ore . In the world, it lies at the very bottom, just above bedrock, in very small, very rare veins. With the base pack, the whole diamond zone is in deep stone: so this is the variant you'll find while exploring. Usage A decorative block for now, and the most prestigious of all. It can't be harvested yet : in creative, breaking it makes it vanish. Behaviour A f"},{"t":"Deep Gold Ore","u":"blocks/strata/deep_gold_ore.html","s":"Description Gold in deep stone: yellow nuggets that stand out all the more against the dark background. A little treasure of the depths. Obtaining In creative: the Natural tab of the inventory, or /give deep_gold_ore . In the world, it replaces gold ore wherever a vein runs through deep stone. It's the form in which you'll meet gold most often. Usage A decorative block for now. It can't be harvested yet : in creative, breaking it makes it vanish. Behaviour A full, opaque, motionless block, from the deep stone family, and harder than ordinary gold ore (which will matter in survival). Tips The c"},{"t":"Deep Iron Ore","u":"blocks/strata/deep_iron_ore.html","s":"Description Iron from the depths: rusty flecks on a deep stone background. Harder to spot than its stone cousin, but just as promising. Obtaining In creative: the Natural tab of the inventory, or /give deep_iron_ore . In the world, it replaces iron ore wherever a vein runs through deep stone, in the depths of every biome. Usage A decorative block for now. It can't be harvested yet : in creative, breaking it makes it vanish. Behaviour A full, opaque, motionless block, from the deep stone family, and harder than ordinary iron ore (which will matter in survival). Tips In deep caves, iron is one o"},{"t":"Deep Stone","u":"blocks/strata/deep_stone.html","s":"Description Darker and denser than ordinary stone, deep stone tells you that you are seriously far below the surface. It looks a bit grumpy; that's only because it carries the rest of the world on its back. Obtaining In creative: the Natural tab of the inventory, or /give deep_stone . In the world, it replaces stone below a certain depth, in every biome. The border between the two isn't perfectly flat: it wobbles by a few blocks. Further down still, you reach bedrock. Usage Dark-toned building, cellar floors, contrast with pale stone. It's also the rock that hosts the deep variants of the ores"},{"t":"Diamond Ore","u":"blocks/strata/diamond_ore.html","s":"Description Stone studded with sparkling sky-blue crystals: diamond, the rarest and most coveted of ores. Finding it is a bit like finding a four-leaf clover underground. Obtaining In creative: the Natural tab of the inventory, or /give diamond_ore . In the world, diamond is only found at the very bottom, just above bedrock, in very small veins. With the base pack, that whole zone lies in deep stone: so you'll almost always meet deep diamond ore there, and rarely if ever this stone version. It remains available for building and for packs that change the world's layers. Usage A decorative block"},{"t":"Dirt","u":"blocks/strata/dirt.html","s":"Description Good old dirt: brown, crumbly, comforting. It hides under the grass and smells lovely after the rain (well, it will, once it rains). Obtaining In creative: the Natural tab of the inventory, or /give dirt . In the world, it forms a layer a few blocks thick under the surface of plains, forests, mountains and snowy tundra, between the grass and the stone. It's also the bottom face of grass blocks. Usage Earthworks, artificial hills, first makeshift huts. It goes down anywhere and comes off just as fast. Behaviour A full, opaque, motionless block. For now, dirt stays dirt: grass doesn'"},{"t":"Fern","u":"blocks/strata/fern.html","s":"Description A fern with finely cut fronds, fond of shade and coolness. It looks ancient, and it probably is. Obtaining In creative: the Plants tab of the inventory, or /give fern . In the world, it is found in clumps in forests , and a few in the snowy tundra , on grass (snowy or not). Usage Decorating gardens, meadows and path edges; a touch of life around your builds. Behaviour A crossed plant: two crossing planes, visible from every side. It has no collision (you walk through it) and hides no neighbouring block. You can aim at it and break it in one hit; it does not grow or spread after the"},{"t":"Ferrous Rock","u":"blocks/strata/ferrous_rock.html","s":"Description A rust-coloured red-brown rock, as if the stone had spent centuries in the rain. It makes up the body of giant iron deposits. Obtaining In creative: the Natural tab of the inventory, or /give ferrous_rock . In the world, it is found in giant iron deposits, rare and rich, stretching for dozens of blocks underground. A few blocks sometimes crop out on the surface, right above. Usage A building block for now, with a warm, earthy tone. Behaviour A full, opaque, motionless block, a little harder than stone. Tips A patch of rust in a meadow is never an accident: an iron deposit sleeps so"},{"t":"Fir Needles","u":"blocks/strata/fir_leaves.html","s":"Description Deep green fir needles, packed into dense sprigs. They smell of winter and give the mountains their greeting-card silhouette. Obtaining In creative: the Natural tab of the inventory, or /give fir_leaves . In the world, they form the cone-shaped crown of firs, on mountain slopes and in the snowy tundra. Usage Hand-made festive trees, evergreen hedges, chalet roofs, artificial alpine forests. Behaviour A solid but see-through block: you can see through the gaps between the sprigs, neighbouring needles included. Like oak leaves, they don't fall when you cut the trunk, and you can walk"},{"t":"Fir Log","u":"blocks/strata/fir_log.html","s":"Description A fir trunk, darker and slimmer than an oak's, with deeply furrowed bark. It has spent its whole life in the cold and it shows: this log has character. Obtaining In creative: the Natural tab of the inventory, or /give fir_log . In the world, it forms the trunks of firs, which grow on mountain slopes and, more sparsely, in the snowy tundra. They take root on grass blocks, snowy or not. Usage Chalets, mountain huts, dark beams that contrast with pale planks. Laid on its side, it makes lovely railings. Behaviour A full, opaque block. Like every log, it is oriented : upright when place"},{"t":"Fir Planks","u":"blocks/strata/fir_planks.html","s":"Description Dark brown fir planks with tight grain, smelling sweetly of resin and mountain chalets. Darker than oak planks, they give character to any room. Obtaining In creative: the Building tab of the inventory, or /give fir_planks . They don't appear in nature; the creative inventory is their only source until crafting arrives. Usage Chalets, imaginary libraries, hulls of boats that never leave the dock, dark rafters. They go very well with stone and sandstone. Behaviour A full, opaque, motionless block. Like oak planks, they neither burn nor rot for now. Tips A fir-plank roof on stone wal"},{"t":"Fire","u":"blocks/strata/fire.html","s":"Description Bright flames dancing above the ground. Fire gives as much light as glowstone, warms the mood… and devours wood. How to get it It has no item: light it with flint and steel (Tools tab of the creative inventory), right clicking a face. Behaviour Gives light of level 15 . It is not solid: you walk through it, and placing a block in its place removes it. It stands on a solid block or next to a flammable one, never next to water. It ages : with nothing to burn around, it soon dies out; otherwise it spreads to the logs, planks, leaves, grass and flowers nearby, which end up consumed. Th"},{"t":"Glass","u":"blocks/strata/glass.html","s":"Description A clear pane with a thin frame, through which you can admire the landscape without catching a cold. Glass is the promise of a bright, airy home. Obtaining In creative: the Building tab of the inventory, or /give glass . It never appears in nature: it's a builder's product through and through. Usage Windows, glass roofs, greenhouses, aquariums, underwater observatories. Anything that needs to see outside (or inside). Behaviour A solid, transparent block: only its frame is drawn, the rest lets everything show through. You can walk on it without trouble. Two glass blocks side by side "},{"t":"Glowstone","u":"blocks/strata/glowstone.html","s":"Description A golden stone full of glowing grains, as warm to the eye as a fireplace. Obtaining In creative: the Building tab of the inventory, or /give glowstone . It isn't found in nature yet. Usage Glowing ceilings, lit floors, lighthouses: anywhere the light should be part of the wall. Behaviour A full, solid block giving off light of level 15 . Like stone, it stops light coming from elsewhere, but shines its own all around. Tips Set into a ceiling or a floor, it gives light with nothing sticking out. Discovery in game It's waiting for you in the Building tab. Aim at it to read its name at"},{"t":"Gold Ore","u":"blocks/strata/gold_ore.html","s":"Description Stone gleaming with little bright-yellow nuggets: gold, gold! The kind of block that makes you squeal with joy around a cave bend. Obtaining In creative: the Natural tab of the inventory, or /give gold_ore . In the world, gold hides in the lower half of the world, in veins smaller and rarer than iron's. Since its heights mostly dip into deep stone, you'll meet it far more often in its deep form; in stone, it only shows up in a thin band just above the deep layer. Usage A decorative block for now, and what a decoration! Ores can't be harvested yet : breaking it in creative makes it "},{"t":"Grass Block","u":"blocks/strata/grass_block.html","s":"Description The grass block is the world's green carpet: neatly mown grass on top, a green fringe spilling over the sides, and dirt underneath. It makes you want to have a picnic. Obtaining In creative: the Natural tab of the inventory, or /give grass_block . In the world, it covers the ground of plains, forests and mountains, until the stone and snow of the peaks take over. By the water's edge, it gives way to shoreline sand or gravel. Usage Gardens, lawns, green roofs. It's also where oaks and firs take root when the world is generated. Behaviour A full, opaque block, with different textures"},{"t":"Gravel","u":"blocks/strata/gravel.html","s":"Description A cheerful jumble of little pebbles, grey, beige and brown. Gravel never quite managed to become stone, but it kept its good mood. Obtaining In creative: the Natural tab of the inventory, or /give gravel . In the world, it carpets the ocean floor and forms the shores and shallow beds along forests, mountains and snowy tundra. Usage Garden paths, mountain trails, the banks of an artificial river. It gives a natural, slightly rustic look to anything it touches. Behaviour A full, opaque block. Like sand, it doesn't fall yet : until gravity arrives, it stays perched wherever you put it"},{"t":"Ice","u":"blocks/strata/ice.html","s":"Description Water that got a little too chilly. Ice is translucent and bluish, hinting at what lies beneath, like a display case laid over the lake. Obtaining In creative: the Natural tab of the inventory, or /give ice . In the world, it covers the surface of the snowy tundra's waters: a single layer, at sea level, with liquid water right underneath. Usage Skating rinks (no sliding yet), frosted windows, snow palaces. It also forms a natural bridge to walk across frozen lakes. Behaviour A solid, translucent block: you can see through it, slightly tinted. It's safe to walk on. It doesn't melt a"},{"t":"Iron Ore","u":"blocks/strata/iron_ore.html","s":"Description Stone sprinkled with small rust-coloured and beige flecks: iron. Low-key but widespread, it's the serious member of the gang, the one that will go far. Obtaining In creative: the Natural tab of the inventory, or /give iron_ore . In the world, it forms small veins in stone, over a wide range of heights, from the depths to well up under the hills. A little less common than coal. In deep stone, it becomes deep iron ore. Usage A decorative block for now: ores can't be harvested yet , and breaking one in creative simply makes it vanish. It will come into its own with survival. Behaviour"},{"t":"Jungle Leaves","u":"blocks/strata/jungle_leaves.html","s":"Description Deep, dense green foliage, full of little holes the sky shines through. Obtaining In creative: the Natural tab of the inventory, or /give jungle_leaves . In the world, they form the crown of jungle trees in jungles . Usage Hedges, green roofs, gardens and tree houses in jungle colours. Behaviour A solid but see-through block. For now, leaves do not fall when you cut the trunk. Tips Their shade stands out from afar: handy to spot these trees from a hilltop. Discovery in game Aim at a tree crown to read its name, or search for \"leaves\" in the creative inventory. Generation In the veg"},{"t":"Jungle Log","u":"blocks/strata/jungle_log.html","s":"Description A jungle trunk with rough greenish-brown bark, with warm and pinkish rings at each end. Obtaining In creative: the Natural tab of the inventory, or /give jungle_log . In the world, it forms the trunks of jungle trees in jungles : a tree huge, with a two-by-two trunk rising up to nearly thirty blocks under a very wide crown hung with vines. Usage Beams, pillars, timber frames and cabins, with a colour of its own to vary your builds. Behaviour A full, opaque block. Like every log, it is oriented : placed on the top or bottom of a block, it stands upright; placed against the side of a"},{"t":"Jungle Planks","u":"blocks/strata/jungle_planks.html","s":"Description Neatly lined-up jungle planks of warm and pinkish wood. Obtaining In creative: the Building tab of the inventory, or /give jungle_planks . They are not found in the world: this is a building block. Usage Floors, walls, decks and timber frames; their colour sets them apart from oak and fir planks. Behaviour A full, opaque block. Tips A floor alternating two woods instantly makes a room look tidy. Discovery in game Search for \"planks\" in the creative inventory. History 0.2.0 Added"},{"t":"Lantern","u":"blocks/strata/lantern.html","s":"Description A small iron cage whose golden heart glows without flickering. Sturdier and brighter than a torch, it gives homes a cosy evening feel. Obtaining In creative: the Building tab of the inventory, or /give lantern . It isn't found in nature. Usage Lighting houses, squares and bridges, where a torch would look too humble. Behaviour Gives off the strongest light, level 15 , which drops by one level per block travelled. It isn't solid. It stands on a solid block or hangs under a block from its little chain, depending on the face you aim at. Remove the floor or ceiling holding it and the l"},{"t":"Lava","u":"blocks/strata/lava.html","s":"Description Glowing orange molten rock sleeping at the bottom of the world. It makes for splendid underground lakes… best admired from a distance. Obtaining Lava has no item of its own: in creative, the lava bucket (Tools tab) pours a source, and the empty bucket takes it back. In the world, it fills caves, caverns and ravines at the very bottom, near the bedrock, in lakes with a flat surface. Usage Scenery of the depths and a landmark: when you see it, the bedrock is not far below. Behaviour Lava flows , but slowly (one block every 1.5 seconds) and not far: 3 blocks on flat ground, downwards "},{"t":"Lavender","u":"blocks/strata/lavender.html","s":"Description A few stems of lavender with purple spikes. You can easily imagine their scent, since you can't smell it. Obtaining In creative: the Plants tab of the inventory, or /give lavender . In the world, it is found in the flower patches of the plains , rarer than the other flowers. Usage Decorating gardens, meadows and path edges; a touch of life around your builds. Behaviour A crossed plant: two crossing planes, visible from every side. It has no collision (you walk through it) and hides no neighbouring block. You can aim at it and break it in one hit; it does not grow or spread after th"},{"t":"Mud","u":"blocks/strata/mud.html","s":"Description Dark, sticky mud that makes lovely squelching noises when you walk in it (well, once sounds arrive). Obtaining In creative: Nature tab of the inventory, or /give mud . In the world, it lines the floor and low banks of swamps. Usage Swamp floors, wet gardens, stilt-house scenery. Behaviour Full, opaque, soft block. Tips Where the mud starts, the shallow water starts: handy for following a swamp's edge. Discovery in game Aim at it to read its name at the top of the screen. Generation Under water: Swamp History 0.2.0 Added"},{"t":"Mushroom Stem","u":"blocks/strata/mushroom_stem.html","s":"Description The pale, fibrous stem of a giant mushroom, soft like damp cardboard (but nicer). Obtaining In creative: the Natural tab of the inventory, or /give mushroom_stem . In the world, it holds up the cap of giant red and brown mushrooms. Usage Pale columns, pillars for mushroom houses, unusual fences. Behaviour A full, opaque, soft block: it breaks quickly. Tips Add a red or brown cap on top and you have your own giant mushroom. Discovery in game Aim at the stem of a giant mushroom to read its name at the top of the screen. Generation In the vegetation: Mushroom Fields History 0.2.0 Adde"},{"t":"Mycelium","u":"blocks/strata/mycelium.html","s":"Description Dirt covered in a mauve felt of mushroom threads. Soft underfoot, a little mysterious. Obtaining In creative: Nature tab of the inventory, or /give mycelium . In the world, it covers the rare mushroom fields. Usage Mushroom gardens, fairy floors, mushroom-house scenery. Behaviour Full, opaque block; the underside is dirt. Tips Giant and small mushrooms happily grow on it. Discovery in game Aim at it to read its name at the top of the screen. Generation On the surface: Mushroom Fields History 0.2.0 Added"},{"t":"Oak Leaves","u":"blocks/strata/oak_leaves.html","s":"Description Bushy, bright green oak foliage, full of little gaps through which you can glimpse the sky. Perfect for a nap in the shade (symbolic shade, until light arrives). Obtaining In creative: the Natural tab of the inventory, or /give oak_leaves . In the world, they form the rounded crown of oaks, in plains and forests. Usage Hedges, bushes, green roofs, garden mazes, camouflaged tree houses. Behaviour A solid but see-through block: you can see through the gaps in the foliage, neighbouring leaves included. For now, leaves don't fall when you cut the trunk: a tree without its log proudly k"},{"t":"Oak Log","u":"blocks/strata/oak_log.html","s":"Description A handsome oak trunk with rough brown bark and clearly visible rings at each end. It smells of forests and childhood tree houses. Obtaining In creative: the Natural tab of the inventory, or /give oak_log . In the world, it forms the trunks of oaks, scattered in the plains and packed tightly in forests. Oaks only grow on grass blocks. Usage Beams, pillars, timber frames, window frames, rustic cabins. Laid on its side, it makes great lintels and garden benches. Behaviour A full, opaque block. The log is oriented : placed on the top or bottom of a block, it stands upright; placed agai"},{"t":"Oak Planks","u":"blocks/strata/oak_planks.html","s":"Description Oak planks in a warm golden brown, nicely planed, with even grain. The building wood par excellence: you already want to lay a rug on them. Obtaining In creative: the Building tab of the inventory, or /give oak_planks . They don't appear in nature. Until crafting arrives, the creative inventory is their only source. Usage Floors, walls, roofs, imaginary furniture, cosy houses. Paired with oak logs, they give an instant cottage look. Behaviour A full, opaque, motionless block. It neither burns nor rots for now: your wooden houses are safe from everything except your own renovations."},{"t":"Obsidian","u":"blocks/strata/obsidian.html","s":"Description A glassy, purplish-black rock born where water meets lava. Very hard, it gleams softly when the light grazes it. Obtaining Pour water onto a lava source (or let water flow to it): the lava sets into obsidian. It is also in the creative inventory (Natural tab). Usage Building and dark decoration. Its great hardness will matter once mining takes time (v0.3). Behaviour A full solid block, like stone. It neither flows nor melts. Tips To set a lava lake, let water flow over it: sources turn into obsidian, flowing lava into stone. Discovery in game You find it by watching water meet lava"},{"t":"Orange Terracotta","u":"blocks/strata/orange_terracotta.html","s":"Description Fine-grained bright orange terracotta, baked by centuries of sunshine. Obtaining In creative: Nature tab of the inventory, or /give orange_terracotta . In the world, it forms layers in the slopes and underground of the badlands. Usage Warm-coloured walls, friezes, patterns: with its coloured cousins, it makes a real builder's palette. Behaviour Full, opaque block, a bit harder than dirt. Tips Each colour stays at the same height along a slope: follow the band you want. Discovery in game Aim at a badlands layer to read its name at the top of the screen. History 0.2.0 Added"},{"t":"Podzol","u":"blocks/strata/podzol.html","s":"Description Brown earth covered in fir needles and dead leaves, smelling nicely of cold forest. Obtaining In creative: Nature tab of the inventory, or /give podzol . In the world, it covers the ground of taigas. Usage Undergrowth, forest trails, rustic gardens. Behaviour Full, opaque block; the underside is dirt. Firs, ferns and mushrooms grow on it. Tips Brown ground under packed firs: you're in a taiga. Discovery in game Aim at it to read its name at the top of the screen. Generation On the surface: Taiga History 0.2.0 Added"},{"t":"Poppy","u":"blocks/strata/poppy.html","s":"Description A bright red poppy with a dark heart, dotting the meadows with little scarlet specks. Obtaining In creative: the Plants tab of the inventory, or /give poppy . In the world, it is found in the flower patches of the plains , mixed with the other flowers. Usage Decorating gardens, meadows and path edges; a touch of life around your builds. Behaviour A crossed plant: two crossing planes, visible from every side. It has no collision (you walk through it) and hides no neighbouring block. You can aim at it and break it in one hit; it does not grow or spread after the world is generated. T"},{"t":"Test Portal","u":"blocks/strata/portal.html","s":"Description A purple veil that swirls gently and glows in the dark. This test portal is purely decorative: it leads nowhere (for now). How to get it In the creative inventory, Building tab. Behaviour Gives light of level 11 . You walk through it and see through it. Its texture is animated ; the \"Animated textures\" graphics setting freezes it. Tips Several portals side by side make a single sheet: the shared faces are not drawn. Discovering it in game Place one in a dark cave and watch the purple glow on the stone. History 0.2.0 Added"},{"t":"Red Mushroom","u":"blocks/strata/red_mushroom.html","s":"Description A red mushroom with white spots, straight out of a picture book. Nice to look at, not necessarily to taste. Obtaining In creative: the Plants tab of the inventory, or /give red_mushroom . In the world, it is found in small groups in forests , with brown mushrooms. Usage Decorating gardens, meadows and path edges; a touch of life around your builds. Behaviour A crossed plant: two crossing planes, visible from every side. It has no collision (you walk through it) and hides no neighbouring block. You can aim at it and break it in one hit; it does not grow or spread after the world is "},{"t":"Red Mushroom Block","u":"blocks/strata/red_mushroom_block.html","s":"Description A piece of a giant mushroom cap, bright red with white spots. It makes you want to sit underneath. Obtaining In creative: the Natural tab of the inventory, or /give red_mushroom_block . In the world, it forms the domed cap of giant red mushrooms, in the giant mushroom lands. Usage Round roofs, gnome houses, very eye-catching garden decorations. Behaviour A full, opaque, soft block: it breaks quickly. Tips Put it on mushroom stems to build your own giant mushrooms. Discovery in game Aim at a giant mushroom cap to read its name at the top of the screen. Generation In the vegetation: "},{"t":"Red Sand","u":"blocks/strata/red_sand.html","s":"Description Orange-red sand, warmed by the sun of the badlands. Obtaining In creative: Nature tab of the inventory, or /give red_sand . In the world, it covers the flat tops of the badlands. Usage Colourful deserts, paths, Mars-inspired gardens. Behaviour Full, opaque block. Like regular sand, it doesn't fall yet. Tips A few blocks under the red sand, the terracotta strata of the badlands begin. Discovery in game Aim at it to read its name at the top of the screen. Generation On the peaks: Warm mountains Below the surface: Badlands On the surface: Badlands Under water: Badlands History 0.2.0 A"},{"t":"Red Terracotta","u":"blocks/strata/red_terracotta.html","s":"Description Fine-grained brick red terracotta, baked by centuries of sunshine. Obtaining In creative: Nature tab of the inventory, or /give red_terracotta . In the world, it forms layers in the slopes and underground of the badlands. Usage Warm-coloured walls, friezes, patterns: with its coloured cousins, it makes a real builder's palette. Behaviour Full, opaque block, a bit harder than dirt. Tips Each colour stays at the same height along a slope: follow the band you want. Discovery in game Aim at a badlands layer to read its name at the top of the screen. History 0.2.0 Added"},{"t":"Sand","u":"blocks/strata/sand.html","s":"Description Golden sand, fine and warm, the kind that makes you want to kick off your shoes. You find it where it's hot and where there's water, which is convenient for a holiday. Obtaining In creative: the Natural tab of the inventory, or /give sand . In the world, it covers the whole desert (with sandstone underneath) and the land rising out of the ocean. It also forms the beaches and the shallow bed along plains and desert shores. Usage Beaches, zen gardens, giant sandcastles. It's also the only ground cacti grow on. Behaviour A full, opaque block. For now, sand doesn't fall : gravity hasn'"},{"t":"Sandstone","u":"blocks/strata/sandstone.html","s":"Description Sandstone is sand that took its time to settle down. Its sides show pretty horizontal layers, and its top is as smooth as a temple floor tile. Obtaining In creative: the Natural tab of the inventory, or /give sandstone . In the world, it forms a layer a few blocks thick right under the desert sand, before the stone. Usage Desert architecture, pyramids, colonnades, bathhouses. It goes beautifully with sand and fir planks. Behaviour A full, opaque, motionless block. The top and bottom faces differ from the sides, giving striped walls and plain floors. Unlike sand, it will never need "},{"t":"Snow Block","u":"blocks/strata/snow_block.html","s":"Description A block of tightly packed snow, dazzling white with bluish glints. It crunches just from looking at it. Obtaining In creative: the Natural tab of the inventory, or /give snow_block . In the world, it caps the highest mountain peaks, above the band of bare stone. Careful: the snowy tundra is covered with snowy grass blocks, not snow blocks. Usage Monumental snowmen, igloos, high-altitude chalets, or simply artificial peaks for mountains of your own. Behaviour A full, opaque, motionless block. For now it never melts, not even placed in the middle of the desert: this is snow of rare d"},{"t":"Snowy Grass Block","u":"blocks/strata/snowy_grass_block.html","s":"Description A grass block wearing its woolly hat: a layer of snow on top, grass peeking shyly out of the sides, and dirt underneath. It's cold out there, but it looks perfectly cosy. Obtaining In creative: the Natural tab of the inventory, or /give snowy_grass_block . In the world, it forms the ground of the snowy tundra. Near the frozen water, the shores are made of gravel. Usage Winter landscapes, mountain villages, very early holiday decorations. The tundra's firs take root on it. Behaviour A full, opaque block, with snow on top, mixed snow-and-grass sides and dirt underneath. For now, the "},{"t":"Stone","u":"blocks/strata/stone.html","s":"Description Stone is the backbone of the world: grey, sturdy, dependable. Dig through a few blocks of dirt, sand or snow and there it is, going on for a long, long way down. Obtaining In creative, it waits for you in the Natural tab of the inventory, or through /give stone . In the world, it forms the core of every biome, under the surface layer. On the highest mountains it even pokes out into the open air, before snow takes over. Further down, it gives way to deep stone. Usage The all-purpose building block: walls, foundations, towers that tickle the clouds. It also hosts the ore veins. Behav"},{"t":"Tall Grass","u":"blocks/strata/tall_grass.html","s":"Description Blades of grass sticking proudly out of the ground, just tall enough to tickle your ankles. The green carpet of the meadows, in relief. Obtaining In creative: the Plants tab of the inventory, or /give tall_grass . In the world, it is found in the tufts covering plains , forests and, more rarely, mountains , always on a grass block. Usage Decorating gardens, meadows and path edges; a touch of life around your builds. Behaviour A crossed plant: two crossing planes, visible from every side. It has no collision (you walk through it) and hides no neighbouring block. You can aim at it an"},{"t":"Terracotta","u":"blocks/strata/terracotta.html","s":"Description Fine-grained orange-brown terracotta, baked by centuries of sunshine. Obtaining In creative: Nature tab of the inventory, or /give terracotta . In the world, it forms layers in the slopes and underground of the badlands. Usage Warm-coloured walls, friezes, patterns: with its coloured cousins, it makes a real builder's palette. Behaviour Full, opaque block, a bit harder than dirt. Tips Each colour stays at the same height along a slope: follow the band you want. Discovery in game Aim at a badlands layer to read its name at the top of the screen. History 0.2.0 Added"},{"t":"Torch","u":"blocks/strata/torch.html","s":"Description A wooden stick crowned with a small flame. The torch is every explorer's companion: wherever it burns, night and caves step back. Obtaining In creative: the Building tab of the inventory, or /give torch . It isn't found in nature. Usage Lighting a cave, a mine tunnel, a house or a path. Leaving a trail of them behind you helps you find the way out. Behaviour Gives off light of level 14 (out of 15), which drops by one level per block travelled and goes around obstacles. It passes through air, water and glass, but not rock. It isn't solid. It stands upright on a solid block , or lean"},{"t":"Verdigris Rock","u":"blocks/strata/verdigris_rock.html","s":"Description A grey-green rock, weathered like an old copper roof. It makes up the body of giant copper deposits. Obtaining In creative: the Natural tab of the inventory, or /give verdigris_rock . In the world, it is found in giant copper deposits, rare and rich, several dozen blocks long. A few blocks sometimes crop out on the surface, right above. Usage A building block for now, with a cool, soft tone. Behaviour A full, opaque, motionless block, a little harder than stone. Tips Greenish stones in the grass or the sand point to a copper deposit underneath. They are easier to spot from afar, fr"},{"t":"Vine","u":"blocks/strata/vine.html","s":"Description A green vine hanging under the foliage, like a garland the forest forgot. Obtaining In creative: the Plants tab of the inventory, or /give vine . In the world, it hangs one to four blocks long under the edge of the crowns of great jungle trees and swamp oaks. Usage Decorating walls, bridges and arches, giving a garden a wild look. Behaviour A crossed plant: two crossing planes visible from every side, with no collision (you walk through it). It cannot be climbed yet. Tips A few vines under a balcony are enough to make it look like a forgotten ruin. Discovery in game Aim at it to re"},{"t":"Water","u":"blocks/strata/water.html","s":"Description The water of seas, lakes and oceans, blue and translucent. It makes you want to dive in, will one day be home to fish, and always looks great on a postcard. Obtaining Water has no item of its own: in creative, the water bucket (Tools tab) pours a source with a right click, and the empty bucket takes it back. In the world, it fills every dip in the terrain up to sea level, from the vast ocean to the small lakes of the plains. In the snowy tundra, its surface is frozen. Usage Scenery, natural border, landmark near the starting point. Behaviour Water flows : a source (the water of sea"},{"t":"White Terracotta","u":"blocks/strata/white_terracotta.html","s":"Description Fine-grained creamy white terracotta, baked by centuries of sunshine. Obtaining In creative: Nature tab of the inventory, or /give white_terracotta . In the world, it forms layers in the slopes and underground of the badlands. Usage Warm-coloured walls, friezes, patterns: with its coloured cousins, it makes a real builder's palette. Behaviour Full, opaque block, a bit harder than dirt. Tips Each colour stays at the same height along a slope: follow the band you want. Discovery in game Aim at a badlands layer to read its name at the top of the screen. History 0.2.0 Added"},{"t":"Yellow Terracotta","u":"blocks/strata/yellow_terracotta.html","s":"Description Fine-grained ochre yellow terracotta, baked by centuries of sunshine. Obtaining In creative: Nature tab of the inventory, or /give yellow_terracotta . In the world, it forms layers in the slopes and underground of the badlands. Usage Warm-coloured walls, friezes, patterns: with its coloured cousins, it makes a real builder's palette. Behaviour Full, opaque block, a bit harder than dirt. Tips Each colour stays at the same height along a slope: follow the band you want. Discovery in game Aim at a badlands layer to read its name at the top of the screen. History 0.2.0 Added"},{"t":"Blocks","u":"blocks/index.html","s":"Building Acacia Planks Birch Planks Bookshelf Fir Planks Glass Glowstone Jungle Planks Lantern Oak Planks Test Portal Torch Natural Acacia Leaves Acacia Log Bedrock Birch Leaves Birch Log Brown Mushroom Block Cactus Coal Ore Copper Ore Deep Coal Ore Deep Copper Ore Deep Diamond Ore Deep Gold Ore Deep Iron Ore Deep Stone Diamond Ore Dirt Ferrous Rock Fir Needles Fir Log Gold Ore Grass Block Gravel Ice Iron Ore Jungle Leaves Jungle Log Mud Mushroom Stem Mycelium Oak Leaves Oak Log Obsidian Orange Terracotta Podzol Red Mushroom Block Red Sand Red Terracotta Sand Sandstone Snow Block Snowy Grass B"},{"t":"Badlands","u":"biomes/strata/badlands.html","s":"Description Hot, arid terraced plateaus of red sand, where every slope reveals strata of coloured terracotta: orange, yellow, white, red. A postcard landscape. Obtaining Badlands appear on the plateaus of hot, dry regions, high above the sea. Usage Red sand and terracotta in five colours, already sorted by nature for your builds. Behaviour Ground : red sand on flat tops, terracotta strata on slopes and under the surface (about thirty blocks deep), gently waving. Vegetation : dead bushes, rare cacti. Tips To gather a given colour, follow its layer along a slope: it stays at the same height. Dis"},{"t":"Beach","u":"biomes/strata/beach.html","s":"Description A strip of soft sand between the sea and the land, ideal for a nap in the sun. Obtaining Beaches line low coasts, where the land slopes gently down to the sea. Steep coasts have no beach. Usage Sand galore and easy access to the water. Behaviour Ground : sand several blocks deep, sand under the shallow water. Vegetation : none. A beach only rises a few blocks above the sea. Tips Follow the beach to go around an island without getting lost. Discovery in game The biome name isn't shown yet: the strip of sand along the water is enough to recognise the beach. Climate Where the biome si"},{"t":"Birch Forest","u":"biomes/strata/birch_forest.html","s":"Description A bright forest of white-trunked birches, sprinkled with flowers and ferns. You can wander here without ever feeling lost. Obtaining Birch forests appear in cool, fairly humid regions. Like the plains, the forest and the flower meadow, it's a biome where the world can make you start . Usage Pale birch wood, flowers to pick and a peaceful setting for a first house. Behaviour Ground : grass on dirt, sand under the water. Vegetation : packed birches, a few oaks, tall grass, flowers, ferns. Tips The white trunks can be seen from afar: perfect for finding your way. Discovery in game The"},{"t":"Deep Ocean","u":"biomes/strata/deep_ocean.html","s":"Description The great depths, far from the coasts: dark water over a gravel floor, sometimes more than forty blocks below the surface. Obtaining Deep oceans fill the open sea, where the continent is furthest away. Usage Gravel, lots of water, and the joy of feeling very small. Behaviour Floor : gravel. Water : static, very deep. Vegetation : none yet. Tips The darker blue of the water marks the great depths: on the world creation map too. Discovery in game The biome name isn't shown yet: F3 shows your altitude, and the floor is far below the surface. Climate Where the biome sits on the climate"},{"t":"Desert","u":"biomes/strata/desert.html","s":"Description A sea of golden sand under a vast sky, where only cacti dare to grow. The desert is hot, dry and surprisingly peaceful. Don't forget your hat. Obtaining The desert appears in hot, dry regions, on rather gentle terrain. Usage Sandstone galore right under the surface, wide open spaces for monumental builds, and cacti for decoration. Behaviour Ground : sand on the surface, then a layer of sandstone, then stone. Vegetation : cacti, which only grow on sand. Shores : sand, on the beaches as well as underwater. No trees, no grass: the contrast with neighbouring biomes shows from very far "},{"t":"Flower Meadow","u":"biomes/strata/flower_meadow.html","s":"Description A meadow covered in flowers of every colour, poppies, dandelions, cornflowers, daisies and lavender, with a few lone trees. A real open-air bouquet. Obtaining Flower meadows appear in temperate regions, between the plains and the forests. It's one of the biomes where the world can make you start . Usage Flowers galore for decorating, and open ground that's ideal for building. Behaviour Ground : grass on dirt, sand under the water. Vegetation : loads of flowers, tall grass, a few bushes, rare oaks and birches. Tips Pick one of each colour: the meadow has five kinds. Discovery in gam"},{"t":"Forest","u":"biomes/strata/forest.html","s":"Description A dense, lush oak forest, where the crowns almost touch and you weave your way between trunks. It smells of moss, bark and adventure. Obtaining Forests appear in temperate, humid regions, on gentle terrain. Along with the plains, the birch forest and the flower meadow, it's one of the biomes where the world can make you start . Usage An endless supply of oak logs and leaves, and the perfect setting for a tree house or an elven village… of your own invention. Behaviour Ground : grass blocks, with dirt underneath, then stone. Vegetation : lots of oaks, packed close together. Shores :"},{"t":"Jungle","u":"biomes/strata/jungle.html","s":"Description A thick, hot jungle where giant trees with trunks two blocks wide tower over an undergrowth of bushes, ferns and vines. Obtaining Jungles appear in hot, humid regions, inland. Usage Jungle wood galore (a single giant tree fills a chest), vines, and a vertical playground for tree houses. Behaviour Ground : grass on dirt, gravel under the water. Vegetation : giant jungle trees with vines, oaks, jungle bushes, ferns, tall grass, a few flowers. The undergrowth is dense: you move slower than on the plains. Tips Climb to the top of a giant tree to scout the area: the canopy can be seen f"},{"t":"Mountains","u":"biomes/strata/mountains.html","s":"Description Dizzying ridges, deep valleys and snowy peaks scratching the sky. The mountains are the biome of breathtaking views and big, slightly mad projects. Obtaining Mountains rise inland, where the terrain is young and barely eroded. They form sharp ridges separated by wide valleys, and they're by far the highest terrain in the world. Usage Lookouts, clifftop castles, tunnels through the rock, and stone cliffs where ores sometimes show. Behaviour Ground : grass blocks on the slopes, with dirt underneath. Altitude : above a certain height, grass gives way to bare stone, then, higher still "},{"t":"Mushroom Fields","u":"biomes/strata/mushroom_fields.html","s":"Description A strange and rare corner of the world, with mauve mycelium ground where giant red and brown mushrooms grow. You feel tiny there, like a bug in a garden. Obtaining Mushroom fields are rare : they only appear where the land is both very humid and very flat, often near swamps. Usage Mycelium, giant mushroom blocks and ready-made architecture for a mushroom house. Behaviour Ground : mycelium on dirt, dirt under the water. Vegetation : giant red and brown mushrooms, lots of small mushrooms. Tips If you find one, note its position (F3): you won't come across them often. Discovery in gam"},{"t":"Ocean","u":"biomes/strata/ocean.html","s":"Description Water, water, and more water. The ocean stretches away from the continents, deep and blue, with here and there a sandy island poking its nose out. Obtaining The ocean fills the regions farthest from inland, where the ground dives well below sea level. Usage Long crossings, underwater bases, lighthouses on sandy islets, and a huge supply of gravel on the bottom. Behaviour Water : static, up to sea level. It doesn't flow and you pass through it like air. Floor : a layer of gravel, then stone. Land above water : sand, on top and underneath. Vegetation : none, for now. Caves never open"},{"t":"Plains","u":"biomes/strata/plains.html","s":"Description Wide stretches of soft grass rolling as far as the eye can see, dotted with lone oaks. The plains are the biome of picnics, long strolls and first houses. Obtaining Plains appear in temperate, rather dry regions, on gentle terrain. They're one of the biomes where the world can make you start (along with the forest, the birch forest and the flower meadow). Usage Ideal building land: flat, open, with just enough trees for decoration. Behaviour Ground : grass blocks, with a layer of dirt underneath, then stone. Vegetation : a few scattered oaks. Shores : sand, on the beaches as well a"},{"t":"River","u":"biomes/strata/river.html","s":"Description A long ribbon of calm water winding between the hills, lined with pale sand. The river crosses the other biomes without asking their permission, and that's a good thing: it ties the landscapes together like a blue thread. Obtaining Rivers form wherever the ground is low enough, whatever the climate around them: they follow long, winding lines across the land. The river biome only covers the bed itself, under the water; the banks belong to the neighbouring biomes. As the terrain rises, the river fades away and leaves only a dry valley carved into the slope. Usage A natural road for "},{"t":"Savanna","u":"biomes/strata/savanna.html","s":"Description A hot, dry expanse covered in tall grass, dotted with acacias with leaning trunks and flat crowns. Obtaining Savannas appear in hot, rather dry regions, between deserts and forests. Usage Orange acacia wood, wide open spaces and a stunning view to build in. Behaviour Ground : grass on dirt, sand under the water. Vegetation : scattered acacias, lots of tall grass, a few bushes. Tips Acacias stand out from afar thanks to their flat crowns: a great landmark in the tall grass. Discovery in game The biome name isn't shown yet: the acacias are enough to recognise the savanna. Climate Whe"},{"t":"Snowy Peaks","u":"biomes/strata/snowy_peaks.html","s":"Description The top of the highest mountains: everlasting snow on ledges and slopes alike, bare rock on the cliff walls, and a breathtaking view. Obtaining Snowy peaks cap the mountains above about 230 blocks high, everywhere but in the hot regions, where warm mountains rise all the way to the top. Usage Snow blocks, stone, and the best viewpoint in the world. Behaviour Ground : snow on ledges and steep slopes (two blocks thick on ledges), stone on the cliff walls. Water : frozen on top. Vegetation : none. Tips Climb up a gentle slope rather than a cliff: the snow covers the places where you c"},{"t":"Snowy Tundra","u":"biomes/strata/snowy_tundra.html","s":"Description A vast frozen plain carpeted in snow, where a few shivering firs stand and lakes freeze into mirrors of ice. Cold, silent and pretty as a postcard. Obtaining The snowy tundra appears in the coldest regions, on gentle terrain. Usage Chalets, igloos, winter villages, and large frozen lakes you can walk across. Behaviour Ground : snowy grass blocks, with dirt underneath, then stone. Water : its surface is frozen into a layer of ice, with liquid water right underneath. Vegetation : a few scattered firs. Shores : gravel along the water. For now, snow doesn't melt and it doesn't snow: th"},{"t":"Swamp","u":"biomes/strata/swamp.html","s":"Description Low, soggy lands where shallow water winds between grassy islets over a muddy bottom. Swamp oaks let their vines dangle, and mushrooms love the place. Obtaining Swamps form in warm, very humid regions where the land is flat and worn down: the ground sinks to sea level there. Usage A good supply of mud and oak wood, mushrooms to pick, and the perfect setting for a house on stilts. Behaviour Ground : grass on the islets, mud under the water only. Water : shallow (a few blocks at most), in pools between the islets. Colours : grass, leaves and water lean olive green, and the fog pale g"},{"t":"Taiga","u":"biomes/strata/taiga.html","s":"Description A cold forest of tightly packed firs, its ground covered in brown podzol and needles, where ferns and mushrooms grow. Obtaining Taigas appear in cold, humid regions, between the tundra and the birch forests. Usage Plenty of fir wood, podzol, mushrooms and a mountain-cabin mood. Behaviour Ground : podzol on dirt, gravel under the water. Vegetation : many firs, ferns, tall grass, small mushrooms. Tips Mushrooms like to grow at the foot of firs: keep an eye on the ground as you walk. Discovery in game The biome name isn't shown yet: the brown ground and packed firs are enough to recog"},{"t":"Warm mountains","u":"biomes/strata/warm_mountains.html","s":"Description The mountains of the hot regions: grassy slopes dotted with acacias, then red sand and bare rock towards the summits. They bridge the temperate mountains and the badlands. Obtaining Warm mountains rise inland, where the terrain is young and barely eroded, in hot and rather dry regions. Usage Acacia wood up high, red sand and stone within reach of your pickaxe, and fine views over the neighbouring badlands. Behaviour Ground : grass on the lower slopes, with dirt underneath. Altitude : around 165 blocks, grass gives way to red sand , then around 200 blocks to bare stone , all the way"},{"t":"Biomes","u":"biomes/index.html","s":"Badlands Beach Birch Forest Deep Ocean Desert Flower Meadow Forest Jungle Mountains Mushroom Fields Ocean Plains River Savanna Snowy Peaks Snowy Tundra Swamp Taiga Warm mountains"},{"t":"/help","u":"commands/help.html","s":"/help [command] Lists the commands, or details one. Run on your screen. Description /help is the console's cheat sheet: it lists every available command, with its syntax and a one-line explanation. Lost? Always start here. Syntax /help : shows every command. /help <command> : shows only the one you asked for (without the slash). Examples /help for the complete list. /help time to remember the time keywords. Behaviour The command is handled directly by your screen, without going through the server, and answers in the language chosen in the options. It works in every game mode. An unknown comman"},{"t":"/tp","u":"commands/tp.html","s":"/tp <x> <y> <z> (~ = your position) Teleports (~5 = 5 blocks further). Run by the server, in creative mode only. Description /tp teleports you instantly to precise coordinates. Ideal for exploring, finding a build again, or taking a close look at a mountain peak spotted in the distance. Syntax /tp <x> <y> <z> . Each coordinate can be: a number (decimals allowed); ~ : your own current coordinate; ~ followed by a number: an offset from your position ( ~5 , ~-10 ). Examples /tp 0 200 0 : off to the centre of the world, well above the ground. /tp ~ ~20 ~ : rise twenty blocks on the spot. /tp ~100 "},{"t":"/give","u":"commands/give.html","s":"/give <item> Puts an item in the selected slot. Run by the server, in creative mode only. Description /give drops an item straight into the selected slot of your hotbar. Quicker than rummaging through the creative inventory when you already know the identifier of what you want. Syntax /give <item> , where the item is an identifier: full, with its namespace: strata:stone ; or short, for the base content: stone is the same as strata:stone . Examples /give glass for a brand-new pane. /give strata:fir_log for a fir log. Behaviour Run by the server, in creative mode only. The item replaces whatever"},{"t":"/gamemode","u":"commands/gamemode.html","s":"/gamemode <creative|survival> Changes the game mode. Run by the server, in creative mode only. Description /gamemode changes the game mode of the current world. In v0.1, only one mode exists, creative ; so the command is mostly here to get ready for the future. Syntax /gamemode <creative|survival> Examples /gamemode creative : switch (or switch back) to creative mode. /gamemode survival : the console kindly tells you that survival arrives in v0.3. Behaviour Run by the server. The chosen mode is saved with the world and appears in the world list. For now, asking for survival changes nothing: th"},{"t":"/time","u":"commands/time.html","s":"/time <set|add|query> [value] Sets the time: set goes on to the next day, noon, night, midnight or tick count; add moves on by that many ticks. Run by the server, in creative mode only. Description /time reads or sets the world clock. Each world keeps its own time, which moves forward on its own during play (except while paused or with /daycycle off ) and is saved with the world. The sky follows it: sun, moon, stars and daylight. Syntax /time <set|add|query> [value] query (or nothing): shows the current time and the day number. set <value> : moves on to the next moment asked for, with a keywor"},{"t":"/seed","u":"commands/seed.html","s":"/seed Shows the world seed. Run by the server. Description /seed shows the world seed: the little secret code from which the whole terrain was calculated. Same seed, same world, every time. Syntax /seed , with no argument. Examples /seed : the console answers with the seed, for instance the word you typed when creating the world. Behaviour Run by the server. It's the only command available in every game mode : knowing your seed isn't cheating. If you typed some text as the seed when creating the world, that text is shown; otherwise, it's the randomly chosen number. Tips Share your seed with yo"},{"t":"/fluids","u":"commands/fluids.html","s":"/fluids [on|off|query|<budget>] Lets water and lava flow or freezes them; a number sets the updates per tick, shared with fire (a fire step counts as three). Run by the server, in creative mode only. Description /fluids lets the world's water and lava flow or freezes them, and sets how many liquid blocks the server updates each tick. The setting is saved with the world; it can also be chosen when creating the world (the \"Liquids\" button). Syntax /fluids [on|off|query|<budget>] on : liquids flow. off : liquids stay as they are, where they are. query (or nothing): shows the current setting. <bud"},{"t":"/fire","u":"commands/fire.html","s":"/fire [spread|destroy] [on|off] or /fire query Lets fire spread or not, and destroy what burns or not. Run by the server, in creative mode only. Description /fire sets how fire behaves in this world. The setting is saved with the world; it can also be chosen when creating it (the \"Fire\" and \"Burning\" buttons). Syntax /fire spread on|off , /fire destroy on|off , /fire query spread off : fire no longer lights new fires around it; it wears out and dies where it is. destroy off : what burns is no longer destroyed (fire still dies out in the end). query (or nothing): shows both settings. Examples /"},{"t":"/daycycle","u":"commands/daycycle.html","s":"/daycycle [on|off|query] Lets the time of day go on or stops it. Run by the server, in creative mode only. Description /daycycle lets the world's time of day go on or stops it. The setting is saved with the world; it can also be chosen when creating the world (the \"Day and night\" button). Syntax /daycycle [on|off|query] on : time goes on, the sun and moon move. off : time stays where it is (handy with /time set to always build in broad daylight). query (or nothing): shows the current setting. Examples /time set noon then /daycycle off : noon forever. /daycycle on : the day goes on again. Behav"},{"t":"/cinematic","u":"commands/cinematic.html","s":"/cinematic <id> Plays a cinematic from the packs. Run on your screen. Description /cinematic plays a cinematic: a scripted camera shot, described in a pack, that sweeps over the surroundings like in a film. The base pack contains a demonstration one. Syntax /cinematic <id> , where id is the cinematic's full identifier (namespace included). Examples /cinematic strata:showcase : the camera rises and circles around where you are. Behaviour Handled directly by your screen, in every game mode. The shot starts from your position : the same cinematic works anywhere. While it plays, you can't move, th"},{"t":"Commands","u":"commands/index.html","s":"Open the console with T or /; Tab completes, up/down recalls commands. /help Lists the commands, or details one. /tp Teleports (~5 = 5 blocks further). /give Puts an item in the selected slot. /gamemode Changes the game mode. /time Sets the time: set goes on to the next day, noon, night, midnight or tick count; add moves on by that many ticks. /seed Shows the world seed. /fluids Lets water and lava flow or freezes them; a number sets the updates per tick, shared with fire (a fire step counts as three). /fire Lets fire spread or not, and destroy what burns or not. /daycycle Lets the time of day"},{"t":"World generation","u":"mechanics/world-generation.html","s":"Principle The world isn't drawn by hand: it's calculated from a seed, bit by bit as you move forward. Same seed, same world, down to the block, whatever order you explore in. It's practically endless: only the border chosen at creation stops it. Terrain and biomes Four invisible maps cover the world: temperature , humidity , continentalness (from open sea to deep inland) and erosion (from flat, worn land to young terrain). The last two give the ground height: deep oceans, gentle hills, ridged mountains. The terrain is fully 3D: cliffs , overhangs and arches where the land is young, terraced pl"},{"t":"Liquids","u":"mechanics/fluids.html","s":"Principle Water and lava flow . Each liquid has sources (the water of seas and lakes, the lava lakes of the depths) and thinner and thinner flows : downwards first, then sideways, heading for the nearest slope. Water that sees a hole 4 blocks away or less flows only towards it: a breach in a lake makes a stream running down step by step, not a sheet; with no hole in sight, it widens in all 4 directions. At the foot of a fall, water is full again and sets off anew. Two neighbouring sources above ground or a source make a third one. Water spreads up to 7 blocks on flat ground, lava only 3, and m"},{"t":"Fire","u":"mechanics/fire.html","s":"Principle Fire is a block of flames that gives light (level 15), ages and spreads. It stands on a solid block or next to a flammable one. At each step (a little over a second and a half), it gets older, may consume a flammable neighbour (sometimes leaving a flame in its place) and light the air around it, up to four blocks above, when that air touches something that burns. The older it is, the less it spreads; a fire without fuel soon dies, and every blaze ends on its own. Flint and steel (creative) In the Tools tab of the creative inventory, flint and steel lights a fire with a right click on"},{"t":"Day and night","u":"mechanics/day-night.html","s":"Principle On Terra, a day lasts 20 minutes : about 10 minutes of daylight and 10 of night, with a short twilight at each sunrise and sunset. The sun rises in the east, crosses the sky tilting a little towards the south, then makes way for the moon . The share of the day and the light left at night come from the dimension's pack, so a pack can change them. What you see The sky goes from daytime blue to the orange of twilight, then to the dark blue of night. The fog and the horizon follow. The sun and moon are big, crisp pixels. The moon has 8 phases , one per day, from full moon to new moon and"},{"t":"Sounds","u":"mechanics/sounds.html","s":"How it works Every sound in the game is made by the game itself from recipes: filtered noise for scuffs and gusts, grains for gravel, snow or leaves, resonances for wood, stone, glass and metal, bubbles for water and lava. Each sound comes in several variants , and each play shifts its pitch a little: two steps in a row never sound the same. What you hear Footsteps : their sound depends on the block underfoot (stone, dirt, grass, sand, gravel, snow, wood, glass and ice, leaves, metal) and their pace on your speed: you can hear running. Broken and placed blocks : each material has its own; glas"},{"t":"Boats","u":"mechanics/boats.html","s":"Principle A boat floats on the surface of water and lava, and never sinks. It comes in oak , fir , birch , jungle and acacia : the hull takes the planks of its wood. In creative, they are in the Transportation tab of the inventory. Placing, getting in, getting off Right click with a boat on water (or on the ground): it is put down, facing where you look. Right click on a free boat: you sit in it. The camera follows the boat, and you can still look around. Sneak (rebindable key, gamepad included): you get off, onto the bank beside it if it is close enough, otherwise on top of the boat. A remind"},{"t":"Saving","u":"mechanics/saving.html","s":"Principle Each world has its own folder: its description (name, seed, mode, play time), your character (position, view direction, hotbar) and a screenshot for the world list. Since the terrain can be recalculated from the seed, only changed areas are saved: a well-explored but barely altered world stays tiny. When the game saves Automatically , at regular intervals (adjustable in Options → Game). With Save and quit , in the pause menu. When you close the game window. On the DS, when you close the lid : instant pause and save. Never a damaged world Each file is written alongside, then swapped i"},{"t":"Game modes","u":"mechanics/game-modes.html","s":"Principle The game mode decides a world's rules. It's chosen at creation, on the \"New world\" screen, and then shown in the world list. In v0.1, only one mode exists: creative . Survival arrives in v0.3. Creative mode The no-strings-attached sandbox, to build and explore in complete freedom: every block is available in the creative inventory, with tabs and search; you break blocks instantly , even bedrock; you fly by double-tapping jump; every console command is allowed; all knowledge is known in advance: there's nothing to discover before you can build. Survival (coming soon) Planned for v0.3."},{"t":"Mechanics","u":"mechanics/index.html","s":"World generation Liquids Fire Day and night Sounds Boats Saving Game modes"},{"t":"Controls","u":"controls.html","s":"Keyboard, mouse and gamepad Strata Mundi plays just as well with keyboard and mouse as with a gamepad , and you can switch at any time. On-screen prompts follow the last device you used: keyboard key or gamepad button. Any keyboard layout The game reads the position of keys, not the printed letter: on a French AZERTY keyboard, movement naturally lands on Z, Q, S, D. Yet the texts show the letter actually printed on your key. The gamepad Buttons are named as on a New 3DS (A on the right, B at the bottom, X at the top, Y on the left), as on the DS handheld console. Left stick to move, right stic"},{"t":"Settings","u":"settings.html","s":"Settings for every machine Strata Mundi's golden rule: everything can be turned on, off or adjusted . Whether you play on a powerful PC, an old laptop or the DS handheld console, you can tailor the game to your machine, your eyes and your habits. Each option comes with a short sentence explaining what it does, performance included. Presets A preset sets all the graphics at once: Very low , Low , Medium , High , Ultra , and DS , designed for the small home-made handheld console. Touching a single graphics setting afterwards switches to Custom , without losing anything else. Applied right away C"}];
